<h1 align="center">MACCA CL</h1>

<p align="center">
  Another attempt at running getting an Xbox Series title to render and run on a Windows PC.
</p>

<p align="center">
  <a href="https://www.buymeacoffee.com/fulger"><img src="https://www.buymeacoffee.com/assets/img/custom_images/orange_img.png" alt="Buy Me A Coffee" height="37" width="170"></a>
</p>

MACCA CL runs the title's x86-64 code natively, supplies the console services
it expects and translates its graphics work to Direct3D 12. It builds on
[VIctory](https://github.com/Marvisak/VIctory), preserving its history and
licence, with selected fixes and a dedicated launcher.

**Development status: experimental, not established as playable.** Static
inspection and import binding pass on the tested local title. World rendering,
complete gameplay and FPS have not been validated by this fork. A successful
build or launch does not establish that the game works.

The November 25 update follows
[fxceless/victory-fork](https://github.com/fxceless/victory-fork) through
`9376fd6`, with selected shader and NVIDIA fixes from its pull requests and
[Zettrox/ztrx](https://github.com/Zettrox/ztrx). It preserves MACCA's guards
and the previous intro-video fixes, adds cross-view texture write tracking,
and names the presentation window MACCA CL. See the
[update notes](docs/UPDATE-2026-11-25.md) for the included PRs, upstream review,
validation and remaining limits.

The follow-up [rendering/performance notes](docs/RENDER-FIXES-2026-11-25.md)
list the shadow sampler, colour view, lane-mask and GPU copy fixes and their
validation limits.

The [model loading follow-up](docs/LOADING-RENDER-FIXES-2026-11-25.md) addresses
stale descriptors, truncated lighting dispatches and texture staging stalls.

## Live controls

- **F5**: show/hide live CPU, GPU memory, FPS and frame-cost statistics.
- **F6**: cycle nine rendering/testing modes, including compatible unlit,
  wireframe and reduced-pass/streaming modes. The mode name appears in red
  at the top left for three seconds.
- **F7**: show/hide the README logo at the bottom left.

Controls are active only while the title window is in the foreground. Testing
modes may produce incomplete images; FPS improvements depend on the workload.
See [controls and mode details](docs/LIVE-CONTROLS.md) and
[upstream changes and validation](docs/HUD-UPSTREAM-2026-11-25.md).

## Download and start

Prebuilt Windows x64 executables are included in
[bin/windows-x64](bin/windows-x64/). Download the repository using **Code →
Download ZIP**, extract it, then:

1. Open **`bin/windows-x64/MACCA CL.exe`**.
2. Use **Sfoglia...** to select your Xbox Series title executable, such as `title.exe`.
3. Press **Avvia con MACCA CL**.

Keep `MACCA CL.exe` and `macca-cl.exe` together. The first is the graphical
launcher; the second is the runtime. The launcher has no engine selector and
always starts MACCA CL with its balanced hardware profile.

You supply your own compatible game files. This repository contains no game
executable, archives, extracted assets or game-derived caches.

| Requirement | Current target |
| --- | --- |
| Operating system | Windows 10/11, x64 |
| CPU | x86-64 with AVX2 |
| Graphics | Direct3D 12 GPU; features required by a shader vary |
| Development tools | Rust/MSVC, Visual Studio C++ tools and Windows SDK |

The development checks used an Intel i7-9700K and NVIDIA RTX 3060. This is a
tested configuration, not a minimum-spec or performance guarantee.

## How the project works

```text
MACCA CL.exe             Choose the game's executable and start the runtime
       │
       ▼
macca-cl.exe             Storage policy, profiles, inspection and execution
       │
       ├── PE loader     Map x64 images, resolve imports, initialise TLS
       ├── HLE services  Supply console APIs and host-compatible services
       └── Graphics      Translate console shaders and commands to D3D12
```

The CPU code runs natively; this is not a CPU emulator or a PC game port.
Console APIs and graphics behaviour still need implementation and validation.

| Directory | Responsibility |
| --- | --- |
| `apps/victory/` | `macca-cl` CLI, title startup and MACCA policy |
| `crates/victory-core/` | Configuration, storage paths and asset policy |
| `crates/victory-pe/`, `victory-loader/` | PE parsing, image mapping, imports, TLS and exception support |
| `crates/victory-hle/` | Console system services, files, input and audio |
| `crates/victory-shader/` | Console shader decoding, translation and DXIL generation |
| `crates/victory-gpu/` | D3D12 command handling, descriptors, resources and host pipelines |
| `crates/victory-formats/`, `victory-game/`, `victory-pipeline/` | Formats, title data readers and pipeline descriptions |
| `launcher/` | Dedicated Windows Forms launcher and its checks |
| `scripts/` | Portable build, packaging and binary verification commands |
| `bin/windows-x64/` | Prebuilt launcher/runtime, licence and SHA-256 checksums |
| `docs/` | Architecture, upstream attribution, validation and asset policy |

Internal `victory-*` names are retained to keep the fork traceable to upstream.
See [architecture](docs/architecture.md) and [upstream provenance](docs/UPSTREAM.md).

## Changes in MACCA CL

- Dedicated single-runtime launcher with one game path and one start action.
- Separate saves and cache, balanced and CLI diagnostic profiles, and a
  per-executable storage key when a title has no manifest ID.
- Bounded snapshots and shader construction memory, reusable texture scratch
  storage, pipeline worker limits and priority for pipelines needed by the title.
- Twelve selected Victory corrections covering buffer/draw bounds, descriptor
  allocation, depth/stencil views, mesh pipeline caching, ANSI paths, shader
  conversions/swizzles/exports and incomplete shader scans.
- Private staging files for pipeline cache writes, with cleanup on failure.

Patch revisions, authors and integration decisions are in
[docs/UPSTREAM.md](docs/UPSTREAM.md). XCL is not bundled or linked.

## Build from source

Install Rust with the MSVC toolchain, Visual Studio or Build Tools with
**Desktop development with C++**, and the Windows SDK. The pinned Rust
toolchain is in `rust-toolchain.toml`. Then run from this repository:

```powershell
.\build.cmd
```

The script discovers Visual Studio, builds the runtime and compiles the C#
launcher with the Windows .NET Framework compiler. Outputs are written to
`dist/MACCA CL/`; no developer-specific toolchain paths are required.

To refresh the executables tracked in this repository after building:

```powershell
powershell -NoProfile -File scripts/package.ps1 -UpdateBundled
powershell -NoProfile -File scripts/verify-bundle.ps1
```

## Command line and local data

```powershell
.\bin\windows-x64\macca-cl.exe doctor
.\bin\windows-x64\macca-cl.exe inspect "D:\Games\XboxTitle\title.exe"
.\bin\windows-x64\macca-cl.exe run "D:\Games\XboxTitle\title.exe"
.\bin\windows-x64\macca-cl.exe run "D:\Games\XboxTitle\title.exe" --execute
```

`run` without `--execute` only maps and binds the images. `doctor` checks CPU
requirements and storage configuration; it does not exercise the GPU.
The CLI also supports shader inspection/translation and a software diagnostic
profile (`--profile diagnostic`).

The default location is `%LOCALAPPDATA%\MACCA-CL`:

| Location | Contents |
| --- | --- |
| `data/` | Runtime state and title saves |
| `cache/` | Derived images, shaders and pipeline cache |
| `logs/` | Launcher-captured stdout and stderr |
| `launcher-settings.txt` | Last selected game executable |

For CLI use, `--storage-root` or `MACCA_CL_HOME` can select an absolute location
outside the source repository. Existing Project Americas local data is not
automatically migrated into this standalone distribution.

## Validation and contributing

```powershell
.\test.cmd
powershell -NoProfile -File scripts/verify-bundle.ps1
```

The runtime validation recorded before packaging reports **381 passed, 0
failed and 6 ignored**. Some GPU/WARP paths and optional compiler tests skip;
they are not coverage. Launcher checks cover argument quoting, runtime
selection, invalid paths, log redirection and the simplified layout.
See [validation details](docs/VALIDATION.md) for scope and limitations.

Contributions should include a focused change, a regression test where
appropriate and the actual commands/results. Keep game files, generated title
data and private paths outside the repository. The owner-approved branding
image and the two built-from-source executables are explicit asset-policy
exceptions; other executables remain excluded.

